  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Connect ordinary rigid joints to the analytic frame sequence and record every frame on device for continuous parity and physical checks.",
  "regressions": [
    "Sixteen scenes cover fixed, spherical, revolute, prismatic, motor, joint/contact and chained joints, one and 120 frames, shared static endpoints in separate colors, and interleaved batches.",
    "Exact all-frame state copies, buffer guards, joint row IDs, solved impulse bounds and disjoint color ownership are verified.",
    "Independent anchor, locked rotation, limit, energy, penetration and motor-target checks reject matching but unphysical reference/target trajectories."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Fixture scene controllers share native dispatch orchestration; every physics stage calls the Rust reference or its mirrored TileLang counterpart.",
    "Native greedy host joint coloring is preserved, including static endpoint ownership. Color and bias uniforms use distinct buffers to satisfy the native adapter ABI.",
    "All-frame diagnostics are currently connected for joint scenes; the original analytic scene suite retains its existing checkpoints.",
    "Ascend source lowering remains separate from unavailable vendor compilation and device execution."
  ],
